gZb(){return"Status comes only from your own data. Each open reminder is checked against today's date and the vehicle's odometer: overdue when its date has passed or its odometer is reached, soon within its lead time, otherwise on schedule; with both a date and a distance, whichever comes first applies. Service kinds show when each was last done and how long ago. There is no health score and no wear estimate: nothing is inferred beyond what you recorded."},
gao2(){return"Totals add up the expense entries in the chosen period; service, fuel and invoice costs are mirrored into the ledger, so each is counted once. Currencies are never added together. Months without spending are shown as zero. Cost per distance = spending in the period \xf7 (highest \u2212 lowest odometer reading dated in the period, from services, fuel and expenses); it is not shown with fewer than two different readings."},
gao1(){return"Average consumption uses the full-to-full method: fuel added after the first full tank up to and including the last full tank, divided by the distance between those two fills. It needs at least two full-tank fill-ups with increasing odometer readings, and every fill-up between them needs an odometer reading; otherwise no figure is shown, with the reason. Cost per distance is shown only when every fill-up in the window has a cost in one currency."},
